//
// Gate E cell: a format-hole `for` over an integer range walks it through an "Iter range" block
// (`n#index` started one below the start), and a filter (`if x > 1`) continues the walk where
// it does not hold, ahead of the body.
// @FR-I-Range: `1..4` walks 1, 2, 3 ([2,4,6]).
// @FR-I-Filter: the `if x > 1` filter keeps only the elements it holds for ([2,3,4]).
// Prints: [2,4,6] / [2,3,4]

fn main() {
  println("{for n in 1..4 {n * 2}}");
  v = [1, 2, 3, 4];
  println("{for x in v if x > 1 {x}}");
}
